   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the New York state energy research and development\nauthority to enter into agreements to establish a New York renewable energy\nlaboratory",
    "basePrintNo": "S4479",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4479-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Energy",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4479\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the New York state energy research and development\nauthority to enter into agreements to establish a New York renewable\nenergy laboratory\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would establish the New York Renewable Energy Laboratory.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one: Legislative findings.\n\nSection 2: Title.\n\nSection 3: Establishes the new York renewable energy laboratory.\n\n  -The New York state energy research and development authority shall\nundertake to establish, through public and private partnerships, which\nshall include New York based colleges and universities, private busi-\nnesses, and not-for-profit entities, a NYREL to be headquartered near\nJFK International Airport in Jamaica, Queens, New York City.  Such labo-\nratory shall be an independent not-for-profit corporation organized\nunder the laws of the state of New York. It shall be governed by a board\nof directors which shall have seventeen members.\n  -The mission of NYREL is to develop renewable energy and energy effi-\nciency technologies and practices, advance related science and engineer-\ning, create jobs, promote economic development and manufacturing, and\ntransfer knowledge and innovations to address the state's energy and\nenvironmental goals.\n  -NYREL shall have an education and training component. NYREL shall\ninclude a goal to recruit minority students, scientists, engineers and\nMBEs in its programs.\n  -NYREL shall seek to develop partnerships especially with CUNY and\nSUNY campuses in Albany, Buffalo, Syracuse, Rochester, Binghamton,\nHudson Valley, Long Island and the city of New York.\n\nSection 4: effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York state is committed to expanding and advancing energy efficiency\nand renewable energy projects to reduce greenhouse gas emissions, reduce\nout of state dependency on fossil fuels, promote public health and\ncreate new jobs. The goal of this act is to make the state of New York a\nnational and global leader in renewable energy research and development.\nNew York State has become the global leader in nanotechnology research\nand development and it can also become the global leader in renewable\nenergy and energy efficiency.  The future of energy, a trillion dollar\nindustry, is renewable energy to achieve cheaper fuel and to prevent\nclimate change. This bill would establish a world-class renewable energy\nlaboratory for the purpose to promote economic growth, create jobs and\nrenewable energy.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2019-2020: 5.6058 REFERRED TO ENERGY AND TELECOMMUNICATIONS\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
