    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Energy",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4479A\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the New York state energy research and development\nauthority to prepare a report on the establishment of a New York renewa-\nble energy laboratory\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would direct the Authority to prepare a report on the estab-\nlishment of a renewable energy laboratory.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one directs the Authority to prepare a report on the feasibil-\nity, costs and benefits of establishing a renewable energy laboratory.\nThe report, at a minimum, shall include: (i) methods to develop partner-\nships with businesses and educational institutions such as CUNY and SUNY\nto support linkages between training, research, development, demon-\nstration and technology transfer resources; (ii) determine whether the\nlaboratory would facilitate the development of renewable energy and\nenergy efficiency technology, as defined in section 66-p of the Public\nService Law; (iii) consider how such laboratory may achieve the goal of\ninvolving minority students, scientists, engineers, and minority and\nwomen owned businesses. The Authority shall submit the final report to\nthe Governor, the Temporary President of the Senate and the Speaker of\nthe Assembly within one year of the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York state is committed to expanding and advancing energy efficiency\nand renewable energy projects to reduce greenhouse gas emissions, reduce\nout of state dependency on fossil fuels, promote public health and\ncreate new jobs. This bill will report on the feasibility of establish-\ning a renewable energy laboratory to help achieve the ambitious goal's\nof the Climate Leadership and Community Protection Act.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
